#2.6 Major Neural Network Types
Connectionist AI relies on Artificial Neural Networks (ANNs), which model cognition using layers of interconnected processing units (artificial neurons) that adjust weighted connections through data.

###Major Types of Neural Networks
* Feedforward Neural Networks (FNN)
To put it simply Feed forward Network is like an asembly line. It is the most basic type of neural network. Where information only moves in one direction, forward. Data enters through an "input layer", passes through one or more "hidden layers" that process the information, and exits as a final decision through an "output layer". Feedforward Neural Network is best for: Simple tasks like identifying if an email is spam or predicting a price based on a spreadsheet of basic data.

* Convolutional Neural Networks (CNN)
To put it simply Convolutional Neural Networks is like scanning a picture with a magnifying glass. CNNs are designed specifically to look at grids of data, like images by scanning small chunks of the image piece by piece. It looks for basic edges and shapes first, then pieces them together. Convulutional Neural Networks is best for: Facial recognition, identifying diseases in medical x-ray, and computer vision for self driving cars.

* Recurrent Neural Networks (RNN)
To put it simply Recurrent Neural Networks is like reading a book amd remembering the last sentence you read. Standard networks forget everything they just did the moment they started a new job ask. RNN solves this problem problem by using a built in "memory" loop that kets them remember previous inputs, so they can understand context in a sequence of data over time. Recurrent Neural Networks is best for: Speech recognition (like alexa, siri, or google), translating sentences between languages, and predicting the weather.


